5 - Files
    -----

    A002_00_Premises.v

      Consolidated arithmetic substrate and A001 import boundary. Defines the
      status/error protocol, canonical A001 destructuring, tagged finite lists,
      arithmetic formula constructors, bounded recognition, implication
      parsing, and elementary constructor/reflection facts.

      The central representation rule is that total A001 projections are never
      interpreted structurally until the enclosing number passes
      `canonical001b`.

    A002_01__Hilbert_Syntax_Checkers.v

      Combined arithmetic syntax, parser, and local-checker layer. Defines line
      codes, K/S/MP tags, guarded tag and line parsers, result projections,
      derivation-line access, and the total arithmetic checkers `check_axk`,
      `check_axs`, and `check_mp`.

      K and S check complete schema shape. MP requires two strictly earlier
      citations and checks antecedent/consequent alignment syntactically.

    A002_02__Normalization.v

      Consolidated verifier, certificate, theorem, and normalization layer.
      Retains `A002_Verify`, arithmetic certificate layouts, deterministic
      diagnostics, and compatibility facts.

      Defines `NormalizedFormula`, `NormalizedRule`, `NormalizedLine`,
      `NormalizedDerivation`, the structural equality and derivation checkers,
      the independent judgments `NormalizedStep` and `NormalizedLines`, and the
      soundness/completeness theorems packaged as `normalized_stepb_iff`,
      `normalized_linesb_iff`, and `normalized_verifyb_iff`. The diagnostic
      traversal `normalized_failure_index` agrees with whole-line acceptance by
      `normalized_failure_index_none_iff`. Defines arithmetic normalization and
      the certified arithmetic entry point with its end-to-end soundness
      theorem and stage-specific rejection classifications.

    A002_94_IO.v

      Arithmetic transport and extraction-facing dispatcher. Defines commands
      for certified verification, independent certificate replay, formula diagnostics,
      and line parsing. Provides result/error decoding and compact `BinNums.Z`
      presentation views.

      This is not the normalization proof boundary; it preserves the serialized
      arithmetic protocol for clients that require it.

    A002_95_API.v

      Stable public import surface. Re-exports the normalized types, checkers,
      reflection theorems, arithmetic compatibility surface, and IO dispatcher
      through one package dependency.

    A002_97_Artifacts.v

      Reproducibility boundary. Redirects `Print Assumptions` for the published
      arithmetic and normalized theorems, then extracts the arithmetic and
      normalized verifier surfaces plus the IO dispatcher to OCaml.

    A002_98_Sanity.v

      Two deliberately small closed computations over normalized syntax: one K
      line and one K/K/MP derivation. Both close by reflexivity and construct no
      nested A001 arithmetic container.

    _appendix/_artifacts/

      Source-side artifact locations for `A002_Verifier.{ml,mli}` and
      `A002_IO.{ml,mli}`. The approved compile bridge generates current outputs
      in its isolated shadow output tree.

    _appendix/_assumptions/

      Source-side report locations for the public theorem surface. The bridge
      emits current redirected reports in the isolated output tree; the
      normalized reflection reports state `Closed under the global context`.

    _appendix/examples/

      Reserved arithmetic example locations. Current effectivity probes live in
      `A002_98_Sanity.v` and operate on normalized inductive syntax.


6 - API
    ---

    The public theorem and executable surface is exposed by

      `From A002 Require Import A002_95_API.`

    Normalized syntax:

      NormalizedFormula : Type
      NFVar             : nat -> NormalizedFormula
      NFImp             : NormalizedFormula -> NormalizedFormula ->
                          NormalizedFormula

      NormalizedRule    : Type
      NRAxK             : NormalizedRule
      NRAxS             : NormalizedRule
      NRMP              : nat -> nat -> NormalizedRule

      NormalizedLine       : Type
      NormalizedDerivation : Type

    Normalized executable checking:

      normalized_formula_eqb :
        NormalizedFormula -> NormalizedFormula -> bool

      normalized_stepb :
        list NormalizedFormula ->
        NormalizedRule -> NormalizedFormula -> bool

      normalized_linesb :
        list NormalizedFormula -> NormalizedDerivation -> bool

      normalized_verifyb :
        NormalizedDerivation -> NormalizedFormula -> bool

    Normalized validity:

      NormalizedStep :
        list NormalizedFormula ->
        NormalizedRule -> NormalizedFormula -> Prop

      NormalizedLines :
        list NormalizedFormula -> NormalizedDerivation -> Prop

      NormalizedProof :
        NormalizedDerivation -> NormalizedFormula -> Prop

    Principal reflection theorems:

      normalized_formula_eqb_eq : forall A B,
        normalized_formula_eqb A B = true <-> A = B

      normalized_stepb_iff : forall prefix rule formula,
        normalized_stepb prefix rule formula = true <->
        NormalizedStep prefix rule formula

      normalized_linesb_iff : forall prefix lines,
        normalized_linesb prefix lines = true <->
        NormalizedLines prefix lines

      normalized_verifyb_iff : forall lines target,
        normalized_verifyb lines target = true <->
        NormalizedProof lines target

      normalized_failure_index_none_iff : forall prefix lines index,
        normalized_failure_index prefix lines index = None <->
        normalized_linesb prefix lines = true

      certified_verify_accept_sound : forall d theta payload,
        A002_Verify_certified d theta = accept payload ->
        exists lines target,
          normalize_derivation d = Some lines /\
          normalize_formula theta = Some target /\
          NormalizedProof lines target

      certified_verify_complete : forall lines target,
        NormalizedProof lines target ->
        A002_Verify_certified
          (encode_normalized_derivation lines)
          (encode_normalized_formula target) =
        accept
          (certified_payload
            (encode_normalized_derivation lines)
            (encode_normalized_formula target))

      certified_certb_iff : forall d theta payload,
        A002_Certified_Certb d theta payload = true <->
        payload = certified_payload d theta /\
        exists lines target,
          normalize_derivation d = Some lines /\
          normalize_formula theta = Some target /\
          NormalizedProof lines target

    Arithmetic compatibility verifier:

      A002_Verify : nat -> nat -> nat
      A002_Certb  : nat -> nat -> nat -> bool

      A002_Verify_certified : nat -> nat -> nat
      A002_Certified_Certb  : nat -> nat -> nat -> bool

      normalize_formula    : nat -> option NormalizedFormula
      normalize_rule       : nat -> option NormalizedRule
      normalize_line       : nat -> option NormalizedLine
      normalize_lines      : nat -> nat -> option NormalizedDerivation
      normalize_derivation : nat -> option NormalizedDerivation

      normalized_failure_index :
        list NormalizedFormula -> NormalizedDerivation -> nat -> option nat
      normalized_rejection :
        NormalizedDerivation -> nat

      encode_normalized_formula    : NormalizedFormula -> nat
      encode_normalized_rule       : NormalizedRule -> nat
      encode_normalized_line       : NormalizedLine -> nat
      encode_normalized_lines      : NormalizedDerivation -> nat
      encode_normalized_derivation : NormalizedDerivation -> nat
      certified_payload            : nat -> nat -> nat

      accept      : nat -> nat
      reject      : nat -> nat -> nat -> nat

    A001 canonical destructuring:

      fst001        : nat -> nat
      snd001        : nat -> nat
      recode001     : nat -> nat
      canonical001b : nat -> bool
      is_pair001b   : nat -> nat -> nat -> bool

    Arithmetic constructors and parsers:

      code_var          : nat -> nat
      code_imp          : nat -> nat -> nat
      code_nil          : nat
      code_cons         : nat -> nat -> nat
      code_derivation   : nat -> nat -> nat
      code_line         : nat -> nat -> nat

      tag_axk           : nat
      tag_axs           : nat
      tag_mp            : nat -> nat -> nat

      parse_imp         : nat -> nat
      parse_rule_tag    : nat -> nat
      parse_line        : nat -> nat
      is_formula        : nat -> bool
      list_exact_lengthb : nat -> nat -> bool

    Arithmetic local checkers:

      check_axk : nat -> nat
      check_axs : nat -> nat
      check_mp  : nat -> nat -> nat -> nat -> nat -> nat

    Arithmetic agreement facts:

      verify_accept_sound : forall d theta p,
        A002_Verify d theta = encode 1 p ->
        A002_Certb d theta p = true

      generated_cert_checks : forall d theta p,
        A002_Verify d theta = encode 1 p ->
        A002_Certb d theta p = true

      A002_Verify_deterministic_export : forall d theta r1 r2,
        A002_Verify d theta = r1 ->
        A002_Verify d theta = r2 ->
        r1 = r2

    IO:

      A002_IO   : A002_IO_Query -> A002_IO_Result
      A002_IO_Z : A002_IO_Query -> A002_IO_Result_Z

      Decode_Result     : nat -> nat * nat
      Decode_Error      : nat -> nat * nat * nat
      Verify_Diagnostic : nat -> nat -> nat * nat * nat


7 - Reproducibility
    ---------------

    The package is registered in the root `_CoqProject` under

      `-Q theories/A002 A002`.

    Rocq is invoked only through

      `_tools/1_compile.command`.

    The bridge performs a cached isolated build under `scratch/shadow`, keeps
    compiled `.vo`, `.glob`, and auxiliary files out of the source theory tree,
    runs the artifact module, and writes its success certificate to

      `_tools/Dump/success.txt`.

    `A002_97_Artifacts.v` reports assumptions for:

      verify_accept_sound
      generated_cert_checks
      check_axk_sound
      check_axs_sound
      check_mp_sound
      normalized_stepb_iff
      normalized_linesb_iff
      normalized_failure_index_none_iff
      normalized_verifyb_iff
      certified_verify_accept_sound
      certified_verify_complete
      certified_verify_accept_payload
      certified_certb_iff
      certified_generated_cert_checks

    The normalized checker datatypes and functions are included in extracted
    `A002_Verifier.ml`:

      NormalizedFormula
      NormalizedRule
      NormalizedLine
      normalized_formula_eqb
      normalized_stepb
      normalized_linesb
      normalized_failure_index
      normalized_verifyb
      normalized_rejection
      normalize_formula
      normalize_rule
      normalize_line
      normalize_lines
      normalize_derivation
      encode_normalized_formula
      encode_normalized_rule
      encode_normalized_line
      encode_normalized_lines
      encode_normalized_derivation
      certified_payload


8 - Notes
    -----

    The normalized layer is the internal effectivity and logical-reflection
    surface. It avoids the rapid numeric growth caused by repeatedly applying
    the Fibonacci pairing function to syntax-tree and list containers.

    The arithmetic verifier remains useful for external numerical protocols.
    It checks a canonical derivation header, an exact tagged-list length, every
    line, and the final target. Rejections use

      encode 0 (encode stage (encode index detail)).

    Legacy accepted arithmetic results use

      encode 1 (encode n (encode theta (encode certs final_formula))).

    Certified accepted results use

      accept (certified_payload derivation_code target_code),

    where both codes have passed normalization and target-sensitive inductive
    verification.

    Certified rejection results retain the same A001-coded error envelope but
    separate input normalization, first failing rule line, empty derivation,
    and final-conclusion mismatch. `normalized_failure_index_none_iff` proves
    that the rule-diagnostic traversal reports no line exactly when the
    normalized whole-line checker accepts.

    `A002_Certified_Certb` is an independent replay checker. It does not invoke
    `A002_Verify` or `A002_Verify_certified`; it checks canonical payload
    binding and reruns only normalization plus the proved structural verifier.

    The arithmetic formula recognizer uses

      formula_bound c = S c.

    This is total and structurally accepted by Rocq, but it is not the preferred
    closed-computation surface. Normalized formulas carry their structure
    directly and require no arithmetic fuel bound.

    `certified_verify_accept_sound` is the arithmetic-to-inductive bridge: an
    accepted public arithmetic result necessarily normalizes to a
    target-sensitive `NormalizedProof`. The legacy `A002_Verify` remains
    available for compatibility, but the IO dispatcher uses
    `A002_Verify_certified`.

    The certified path does not delegate to that legacy verifier. Arithmetic
    normalization is the serialization boundary; all proof-rule execution
    after it is over `NormalizedFormula`, `NormalizedLine`, and ordinary lists.

    `certified_verify_complete` proves the converse for the canonical quotation:
    every `NormalizedProof` can be serialized by `encode_normalized_derivation`
    and `encode_normalized_formula`, and that serialization is accepted.

    `certified_certb_iff` characterizes replay exactly: a payload checks if and
    only if it is the canonical `(derivation_code,target_code)` binding and
    those codes normalize to a `NormalizedProof`.
